{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Do not allow.</b> Why should your mouth give birth to sin and evil upon your flesh, which is your body, if you do not fulfill what you spoke with your mouth. And know that a man's ways are before the eyes of HaShem, and all his steps He counts. And an angel among His attendants is appointed to write in a book all the words that proceed from a person's mouth. And do not say before the angel that it was an inadvertent error, the vow you vowed." "<b>And destroy the work of your hands.</b> Like והשחית, and similar is מחבלים כרמים. There is also חבל in the sense of giving birth, like יחבל און חבלתך אמך, שמה חבלה ילדתך. And it is possible that it is from צירים וחבלים on account of the pains of childbirth, and חבל a third, and כשוכב בראש חבל — this is the mast that is on a ship, upon which all the ropes are suspended; it is an adjective-noun like איש אטר יד ימינו."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved ה׳ as HaShem per standard reverent abbreviation.", 1 "The phrase 'וחבל שלישי' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. Ibn Ezra appears to introduce a third sense of חבל before the mast example."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:44.154928106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}